//@ run-pass
//@ requires: madaros

// Task 1 Step 5: exercises pem_decode_next against a multi-certificate PEM
// bundle -- exactly the shape Task 2 (trust_store.sio) will loop over when
// parsing a system CA bundle. The fixture is the same real openssl cert
// used by pem_decode_roundtrip.sio, concatenated with itself:
//
//   cat cert.pem cert.pem > double.pem
//
// Offsets below were independently confirmed via Python against the exact
// same byte buffer that's hand-transcribed here:
//   pem = open('cert.pem','rb').read()          # 1111 bytes
//   double = pem + pem                          # 2222 bytes
//   end_marker = b'-----END CERTIFICATE-----'
//   pos1 = double.find(end_marker) + len(end_marker)                  # 1110
//   pos2 = double.find(end_marker, pos1) + len(end_marker)            # 2221
//   double.find(b'-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----', pos1)                 # 1111
//
// So: call 1 (start=0) decodes block 1, returns next=1110 (points at the
// '\n' separating the two PEM texts -- NOT -1, since pem_decode_next never
// looks ahead for a following block, per pem.sio's own doc comment). Call 2
// (start=1110) skips that stray newline, finds block 2's BEGIN marker at
// 1111, decodes it, and returns next=2221 (the trailing '\n' at the very
// end of the 2222-byte buffer). Call 3 (start=2221) finds no further BEGIN
// marker before buf_len and returns next=-1: "no more blocks".

